{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "gzEsroaXaE", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 914280, "segment_id": "BtmrQdOYQy", "segment_broadcast_id": "gzEsroaXaE", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Dan Harris (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 914280, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "gzEsroaXaE", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 914280, "segment_id": "LHkoIh3sJx", "segment_broadcast_id": "gzEsroaXaE", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Bill", "segment_description": "(Studio: Dan Harris)  The deal to rescue the American financial system introduced.  \n\n(Capitol Hill: Rachel Martin)  The compromise 700 billion dollar rescue package reviewed; details given of the specifics.  [Speaker of the House Nancy PELOSI&nbsp- says the message to Wall Street is \"the party is over.\"]   [Representative Virginia FOX, Senator Judd GREGG&nbsp- offer differing opinions on the bill.]  The possibility of the bill passing with House Republicans opposed to a government bailout discussed.  \n\n(Studio: Dan Harris)  Report introduced.  \n\n(Studio: Betsy Stark)  The question of whether the huge bailout will work to keep Wall Street from the economic abyss featured; details given of the need to jumpstart the credit market and of the specifics of the economic problems.  [Economic Outlook Group Bernard BAUMOHL&#134;- says we need to restore some health to the banking system.]  [On \"This Week,\" former Labor secretary Robert REICH&#134;, former Speaker of the House Newt GINGRICH&#134;- offer views on the plan.]  [Tuck School of Business professor Robert HANSEN&#134;- says a team of professional finance managers is needed.]  [The Stanford Group policy analyst Anne MATHIAS&#134;- says the government could actually make money.]  [OakBrook Investments CIO Janna SIMPSON&#134;- offers an assessment.]  \n\n(Studio: Dan Harris)  The support from Senator John McCain for the deal noted.  \n\n(Washington: Ron Claiborne)  The recent rough days for McCain as the bailout plan goes forward reviewed; details given about the fallout from vice presidential candidate Governor Sarah Palin's interview with Katie Couric; scenes shown of the \"Saturday Night Live\" satire of Palin.  [On \"This Week,\" McCAIN&nbsp- comments.]  [Political analyst Kevin MADDEN&#134;- assesses the Palin pick.]  \n\n(Detroit: John Berman)  Senator Barack Obama's campaign featured; ABC News/\"Washington Post\" poll figures on who the people trust to handle the economy cited; scenes shown from several Obama rallies.  [Today and yesterday, OBAMA&nbsp- criticizes McCain's finance to the financial crisis.]  [On \"Face the Nation.\" OBAMA&nbsp- says he shaped the provisions to help taxpayers.] ", "segment_duration": 540, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 914281, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "gzEsroaXaE", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-28", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast